      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Back care advice similar to that used in \"low back pain schools' was made available to a group of primiparous women as early in their pregnancy as possible. Subsequently it was shown that they experienced significantly less \"troublesome' and \"severe' backache (P = less than 0.01) than a control group for whom such advice was not available."},
